{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mat-2-1","title":"Matthew 2:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The wise men from the east enquire after Christ; 3 at which Herod is alarmed. 9 They are directed by a star to Bethlehem, worship him, and offer their presents. 13 Joseph flees into Egypt with Jesus and his mother. 16 Herod slays the children; 20 himself dies. 23 Christ is brought back again into Galilee to Nazareth.</p>\n<p>\"Fourth year before the account called Anno Domini.\"</p>\n<p>Jesus. 1:25; Lu 2:4-7 Bethlehem. 5; Mic 5:2; Lu 2:11,15; Joh 7:42 Herod.This was Herod the Great, for an account of whom see the Connection of the Old and New Testaments in the Comprehensive Bible.</p>\n<p>3,19; Ge 49:10; Da 9:24,25; Hag 2:6-9 from. Ge 10:30; 25:6; 1Ki 4:30; Job 1:3; Ps 72:9-12; Isa 11:10; 60:1-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-2-2","title":"Matthew 2:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>born. 21:5; Ps 2:6; Isa 9:6,7; 32:1,2; Jer 23:5; Zec 9:9; Lu 2:11; 19:38 Lu 23:3,38; Joh 1:49; 12:13; 18:37; 19:12-15,19 his. Nu 24:17; Isa 60:3; Lu 1:78,79; Re 22:16 worship. 10,11; Ps 45:11; Joh 5:23; 9:38; 20:28; Heb 1:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-2-3","title":"Matthew 2:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>he. 8:29; 23:37; 1Ki 18:17,18; Joh 11:47,48; Ac 4:2,24-27; 5:24-28 Ac 16:20,21; 17:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-2-4","title":"Matthew 2:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>the chief. 21:15,23; 26:3,47; 27:1; 1Ch 24:4-19; 2Ch 36:14; Ezr 10:5; Ne 12:7 Ps 2:2; Joh 7:32; 18:3 scribes. 7:29; 13:52; 2Ch 34:13,15; Ezr 7:6,11,12; Jer 8:8; Mr 8:31; Lu 20:19 Lu 23:10; Joh 8:3; Ac 4:5; 6:12; 23:9 he demanded. Mal 2:7; Joh 3:10